{"title":"Career Roadmap · Religious Studies Teacher","role":"Religious Studies Teacher","summary":"A Religious Studies Teacher teaches students about religious traditions, sacred texts, history, philosophy, ethics, rituals, cultures and the role of religion in society. Depending on the institution, the role may focus on one tradition—such as Buddhism, Islam, Christianity or Jainism—or on comparative and academic study of multiple traditions.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Buddhist / Islamic / Christian / Jain / Comparative Religion Studies"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest professional profile combines religious studies + pedagogy + academic research + intercultural communication + digital teaching."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Religious Studies","Teaching qualification/subject-specific preparation","Teaching Internship","Religious Studies Teacher","Senior Teacher","Subject Coordinator","Academic Leader"]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Requirements vary substantially between secular schools, faith-based schools, colleges and universities. Some positions require a recognised teacher-education qualification, while faith-based institutions may have additional tradition-specific requirements. Verify the current eligibility rules for the target institution and teaching level."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Religious studies + history + philosophy"}],[{"text":"2027–2028"},{"text":"Skill Building"},{"text":"Pedagogy + comparative religion"}],[{"text":"2028–2029"},{"text":"Professional Preparation"},{"text":"Teaching practice + curriculum"}],[{"text":"2029–2031"},{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Religious Studies Teacher"}],[{"tex